      "message": "\u003e and set it only later in vmx_vcpu_create.\n\nYou mean in attach_pkvm_vcpu_to_vm()?\n\nIndeed, this looks like a problem: the host may successfully create 2 new vCPUs with the same vcpu_id in parallel (since none has been attached to the VM yet, so this validation succeeds for both), and then successfully attach them both in attach_pkvm_vcpu_to_vm().\n\nI think a cleaner way to fix this is to do what I mentioned, among other things, in aosp/4151702: repurpose `created_vcpus` to increment it here at the beginning of vCPU creation, not at the end, and let `attach_pkvm_vcpu_to_vm()` etc use `online_vcpus` instead of `created_vcpus`, thus make the semantics closer to the host KVM (and also, for instance, avoid wasting memory on this `vcpu_ids` bitmap).\n\nAlthough, after more thinking, maybe a simpler and cleaner way is to move this validation of duplicated vcpu_id into attach_pkvm_vcpu_to_vm(), i.e. after vCPU creation. That would make pKVM\u0027s flow even closer to the upstream flow in `kvm_vm_ioctl_create_vcpu()`. Although that would make it affected by the upstream issue we found yesterday (i.e. corrupting pid_table entry of another vCPU with the same vcpu_id). But I have an idea how to fix it: move pid_table entry setup from `.vcpu_create()` to a new `.vcpu_postcreate()` callback invoked at the very end of successful vCPU creation (in particular, in our pKVM case, after successful attach_pkvm_vcpu_to_vm()).",
